Be careful with strong pets in Minetown. Usually you want the some
shopkeepers and the priest alive, and sometimes a pet will attack an armed
watchman and get killed. Leash it, whistle it, watch it's progress with
telepathy, leave it behind on another level (shortly) or lock NPCs that you
care about away. Or lock the pet away.

> So....question 1....where can I get protection now?? Or am I screwed??

There's at least one more guaranteed priest further down (well, a lot
further down, I admit). There might be randomly generated temples (rooms
with an altar and attending priest in the main dungeon). You can get
intrinsic protection from prayer when your luck is right (-> altar
camping).

> Also, during my travels, I found a poly trap and a magic whistle. After
> a few baby dragon pets, I ended up with a Marilith, which seems like it
> might be a good pet. 

A Marilith is nice. Fast, low AC, lots of attacks per round. Give it a
good weapon, it has two weapon attacks.

>                      Neither the Marilith or the Djinni seem to eat
